.TH S3-INVENTORY-BILL 1 "2026-11-19" "s3-inventory-bill 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3-inventory-bill \- estimate S3 storage cost from an inventory CSV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
Estimate S3 storage cost from an inventory CSV. Reads files only, no network.

Usage: s3-inventory-bill [OPTIONS] <FILE>...

Arguments:
  <FILE>...  S3 Inventory CSV files, or gzip-compressed CSV

Options:
      --prices <FILE>                Price file. The default is the built-in US East (N. Virginia) list
      --as-of <YYYY-MM-DD>           Day that ages are measured to, `YYYY-MM-DD`. An object last modified on or before that day is eligible; the time of day is not read. Without it, savings are omitted
      --prefix-depth <PREFIX_DEPTH>  Path segments in the prefix, 1 to 8. `logs/2024/a` at depth 1 is `logs/` [default: 1]
      --json                         Print JSON instead of the text table
      --md                           Print Markdown tables instead of the text table
      --output <FILE>                Write the report to this file instead of standard output. The file is written whole and renamed into place; an existing file is replaced, a symbolic link is replaced and not followed
      --quiet                        Print only the report and errors: no warning copies on standard error
      --verbose                      Also print progress lines on standard error
  -h, --help                         Print help
  -V, --version                      Print version

Exit codes: 0 ok, 2 input or usage error, 130 interrupted (SIGINT).
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
s3-inventory-bill reads one or more local S3 Inventory CSV files and prices the storage per storage class and per key prefix.
For eligible Standard objects it also shows what a lifecycle move to Standard-IA, Glacier Instant Retrieval, Glacier Flexible Retrieval, or Glacier Deep Archive would change.
The transition is priced only; the tool never runs it.
.PP
Every amount is an estimate from list prices, not your AWS invoice; free tier, credits and discounts are not included.
The text report says so in one line, and the JSON has
.B "estimate": true
at the top level.
The monthly cost is named
.B estimated_usd_month
in both.
.PP
A warning names the date of the price file when it is more than 180 days before
.B --as-of
or, without it, before today.
The exit code stays 0.
The environment variable
.B SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
(seconds since 1970-01-01 UTC), when set, replaces the clock for this check.
.PP
It reads files only.
It makes no network call and uses no AWS SDK.
.PP
The first row of every file must be a header line that names the columns
.BR Bucket ,
.BR Key ,
.B Size
and
.BR StorageClass ,
in any order.
.B LastModifiedDate
and
.B IntelligentTieringAccessTier
are optional.
A raw S3 Inventory CSV has no header line, so add one that follows the column order in the inventory's manifest.
A file without it is refused.
Keys are used as written and are not URL-decoded.
.PP
The input is a
.I .csv
file or a gzip
.I .csv.gz
file.
Parquet and ORC are rejected.
A directory is rejected, as is a pipe, a device or any other file that is not a regular file; a symlink to a file is followed, and a file larger than 1073741824 bytes, on disk or after gzip, is rejected.
The same key in two rows is counted twice.
.PP
The built-in rates are the US East (N. Virginia) figures from the Amazon S3 pricing page as read on 2026-11-09.
A storage class outside the quote, such as Reduced Redundancy, is not priced.
Retrieval fees and the account free tier are not part of the result.
Savings assume the object stays for the whole horizon and are not a forecast.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --prices \fIFILE\fR
Read the rates from a JSON price file instead of the built-in list.
The file replaces the whole quote.
It must be a regular file.
An unknown field is ignored, and a duplicate key is an error.
.TP
.B --as-of \fIYYYY-MM-DD\fR
The day that object ages are measured to.
A Standard object last modified on or before that day is eligible; the time of day in LastModifiedDate is not read.
Without it the lifecycle block is omitted and only storage is priced.
The clock is never used as a default.
.TP
.B --prefix-depth \fIN\fR
How many path segments make up the prefix, from 1 to 8.
Any other value is a usage error with exit 2.
The key
.I logs/2024/a
at depth 1 is
.IR logs/ .
The default is 1.
.TP
.B --json
Print one JSON document instead of the text table.
It starts with
.BR "schema_version": 1 .
An error prints no JSON.
Money and byte totals are strings.
With it, warnings go to standard error; in the text table they are lines of the report on standard output, and the price-age warning is also copied to standard error.
.TP
.B --md
Print the same amounts as Markdown tables, with the estimate line, instead of the text table.
A
.B |
or a line break in a name is escaped.
With
.BR --json ,
it is a usage error with exit 2.
.TP
.B --output <FILE>
Write the report to FILE instead of standard output; nothing is printed on standard output.
The report is written to a temporary file in the same directory and renamed over FILE.
An existing file is replaced.
A symbolic link at FILE is replaced and not followed.
A directory, a pipe or a device is refused.
A missing directory is not created.
Any failure is exit 2 with a message on standard error.
.TP
.B --quiet
Print only the report and errors.
With
.BR --json ,
the copies of the warnings on standard error are left out; the JSON still lists them.
The text report is unchanged.
With
.BR --verbose ,
it is a usage error with exit 2.
.TP
.B --verbose
Also print progress lines on standard error, each starting with
.BR s3-inventory-bill: :
the file being read, the number of files being priced, and done.
The report on standard output is unchanged.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print the usage text.
.TP
.B -V, --version
Print the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The report was written.
.TP
.B 2
An input or usage error: an unreadable or unsupported file, an invalid cell, a missing column, a bad option, or standard output that is closed or cannot be written.
The message goes to standard error.
.TP
.B 130
SIGINT.
Nothing is written to standard output, and standard error has the line
.BR "s3-inventory-bill: interrupted by SIGINT" .
A SIGINT during the final write of the report waits until the write is complete.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
s3-inventory-bill examples/inventory.csv
s3-inventory-bill \-\-as\-of 2026\-11\-09 \-\-json examples/inventory.csv
s3-inventory-bill \-\-prefix\-depth 2 part1.csv.gz part2.csv.gz
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
README.md and QUALITY.md in the source tree.
